      "id": "claim_78c7c586d900429793f25006f90cbfa6",
      "statement": "A chat-created gadget or binding edge is real and fully functional in the registry before acceptance, but for reads everything outside the creating chat (mainline loads, other chats, blueprints, use-role sharing) treats it as nonexistent while for writes it still occupies its name; the pending {chatId, sequence} stamp is written in the same transaction as the log message recording it, so the log and registry can never disagree, and an unstamped record from a crashed step is reaped by reconcilePendingGadgets.",
