      "id": "claim_c89a7a2eef4942378a2d5300b280fac5",
      "statement": "mergeChanges always accepts everything the chat proposes (a partial accept would be incoherent under the epoch reset): it materializes live rows, reaps crash-orphans, flattens chat content as of mergeThrough, measures per-gadget change against the chat's merged commit (mainline movement on an untouched gadget neither implicates the chat nor blocks the accept), writes per-gadget commits content-addressedly, and revalidates against head snapshots after every await, returning {outcome: 'stale'} with no partial effects instead of half-applying.",
