      "statement": "Uncommitted code is a per-chat stream: a chat pins each committed gadget it edits at a head commit (validated against the current head or a parent, tolerating one concurrent merge) and applies CodeChanges numbered by per-generation revision; submitCodeChange transforms a submission across anything accepted since, validates it, appends, and broadcasts, with per-(user, clientId, seq) dedupe records holding the landing point and a SHA-256 content digest so a same-seq retry must match byte-for-byte and only the last submission is remembered.",
